We are now interested in stability properties \deleted{of the}\inserted{for the} subcategories \(\underline{\mathrm{Hom}}(B^o,A)\) of \((A\times B)^\wedge\), and \(A\) of \(A^\wedge\). The functor \(p_{B*}\;(=(\Gamma_B)\circ)\) maps \deleted{\((A\times B)'\)} \(\underline{\mathrm{Hom}}(B^o,A)\) into \(A\), as soon as \(B\) admits a final object \(e_B\) (for it then identifies with \(\unsure{\Gamma|E}_{e_B}''\)). Thus we find
\diagram{\begin{tikzcd}
&\underline{\mathrm{Hom}}(B^o,A)\arrow[dl]\arrow[dr,"(\Gamma_A)\circ"]&\\
A^{\deleted{\unsure{\wedge}}}\arrow[dr,"\Gamma_A"']&&B^\wedge=\underline{\mathrm{Hom}}(B^o,(\mathrm{Ens}))\arrow[dl,"\Gamma_B"]\\
&{}&
\end{tikzcd}}
\uline{NB} (We have in mind the case where \(B=\Delta\) e.g. (cat of standard simplices) so \(\underline{\mathrm{Hom}}(B^o,A)=sA\) simplicial objects of \(A\).
\deleted{\unsure{I do not know}}

\deleted{We} We are interested \deleted{\unsure{in the}} in the case where \(\underline{\mathrm{Hom}}(B^o,A)\) is stable under
\[\underline{\mathrm{Hom}}(p_A^*(M),X)\overset{\mathrm{def}}=X^M\qquad\text{for }\forall\ M\in\mathrm{Ob}B^\wedge.\]
\margin{(\unsure{or we restr. ourselves to sets of homot. ends})}
(whereas \(\underline{\mathrm{Hom}}(B^o,A)\) does not nec\unsure{\({}^{\mathrm{t}}\)} contain the \(p_A^*(M)\)\ldots\(^{*}\))

It suffices that \(A\) be stable under \(\varprojlim\) of the types required to represent \(M\) \inserted{as \(\varinjlim\)} in terms of representable functors.
\margin{\figure{\begin{tikzpicture}\draw[->] (0,1.8)--(0,0);\draw[->] (.04,1.8)--(.04,0);\end{tikzpicture}}}
Note that then also
\[
\begin{aligned}
\underline{\mathrm{Hom}}_B(X,Y^M)&\simeq p_{A*}\underbrace{\underline{\mathrm{Hom}}(X,\underline{\mathrm{Hom}}(p_A^*(M),Y))}\\
&\simeq p_{A*}(\underline{\mathrm{Hom}}(X\times p_A^*(M),Y))\\
&\simeq\mathrm{Hom}_B(X\times p_A^*(M),Y).
\end{aligned}
\]
\margin{\(^{*}\) To \unsure{construct|have} \(p_A^*(M)\), it would be necessary that \(\forall b\in\unsure{M|B}\) \inserted{\unsure{(for given b)}}, the \uline{constant} functor on \(A\) with value \(M(b)\) be representable. But this means that \(M(b)\) is reduced to \unsure{one elem.|one element} and \(A\) has final \unsure{objt}. Thus \unsure{OK iff} \(M\) final object of \(\widehat B\), and \(A\) admits final object !!}
